1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,967
Savana, can we talk?

2
00:00:03,968 --> 00:00:05,901
He really looks familiar.

3
00:00:05,901 --> 00:00:07,666
He went viral last week.

4
00:00:07,667 --> 00:00:12,145
They say people were furious at him
because he's a land grabber.

5
00:00:12,145 --> 00:00:14,214
Liam Herrera, land grabber.

6
00:00:14,214 --> 00:00:17,500
Mom, why do many people seem
to be obsessed with Savana?

7
00:00:17,501 --> 00:00:19,199
It feels like I've known her for a long time.

8
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,833
I'm so fond of her.

9
00:00:20,834 --> 00:00:23,033
She's so familiar to me.

10
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:25,567
Savana, I want you
to meet Liam, my boyfriend.

11
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,161
I sympathize with the poor.

12
00:00:28,161 --> 00:00:30,830
So I can't understand how you could do that

13
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:32,599
to the residents of Verde Village.

14
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:34,768
I'm sorry for whatever our company did.

15
00:00:34,768 --> 00:00:36,136
You don't need to explain.

16
00:00:36,136 --> 00:00:38,471
I just want to call you out
because what you did is wrong.

17
00:00:38,471 --> 00:00:40,507
So I'm giving you a second chance, Liam.

18
00:00:40,507 --> 00:00:41,775
Are you reinstating me at Casa Fuerte?

19
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:44,377
No, but I will assign you
to one of the other companies...

20
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:46,712
Blacksmith Productions.

21
00:01:10,137 --> 00:01:12,706
Auntie, have some water.

22
00:01:12,706 --> 00:01:14,340
Son!

23
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,775
Liam.

24
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:17,886
Son!

25
00:01:17,886 --> 00:01:20,080
Goodness...

26
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,783
Congratulations!

27
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:30,057
Via told me that you'll make a film
with Savana in Blacksmith.

28
00:01:30,057 --> 00:01:34,128
Let me tag along when you film it, okay?

29
00:01:34,128 --> 00:01:36,697
- Sure, Mom.
- Okay.

30
00:01:36,697 --> 00:01:39,933
Sorry, I told her before you could.

31
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:42,035
It's good news anyway.

32
00:01:43,170 --> 00:01:45,372
It's okay.

33
00:01:45,372 --> 00:01:48,975
I'll just get the other food in the kitchen.

34
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:51,645
Son...

35
00:01:51,645 --> 00:01:55,049
I'm so happy for you.

36
00:01:55,049 --> 00:01:59,720
You can finally fulfill your dream
of making a film, right?

37
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:03,757
Mom, it's still Vergil's project.

38
00:02:03,757 --> 00:02:05,859
I can't own it.

39
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:07,394
Come on.

40
00:02:07,394 --> 00:02:09,796
It's only for now.

41
00:02:10,564 --> 00:02:15,335
You can make the film you want next time.

42
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:18,104
You can make it according to your taste.

43
00:02:19,039 --> 00:02:25,045
Promise me you'll do your best.

44
00:02:25,045 --> 00:02:28,415
Don't waste this opportunity.

45
00:02:29,349 --> 00:02:33,019
You've wasted a lot of time already.

46
00:02:33,687 --> 00:02:41,294
You're good at construction,
but your heart isn't there.

47
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:50,645
Mom, everything I do is for you.

48
00:02:51,839 --> 00:02:56,844
So I promise that wherever I get assigned,

49
00:02:56,844 --> 00:03:01,548
be it in the construction
or the production company,

50
00:03:01,548 --> 00:03:04,884
I'll do everything to make you proud.

51
00:03:07,354 --> 00:03:09,723
You're just saying that
to make me feel better.

52
00:03:09,723 --> 00:03:11,358
- No.
- No?

53
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:13,727
Oh, boy!

54
00:03:33,901 --> 00:03:36,701
[Batang Bilibid]

55
00:03:42,901 --> 00:03:47,234
[Boy Backflip, by Ramon dela Peña]
[Pretty Boy, by Ramon dela Peña]

56
00:03:50,501 --> 00:03:53,467
[.45 Caliber]
[My Teacher, My Idol]

57
00:04:13,487 --> 00:04:17,390
So you're the core team
of the Tristan-Savana project?

58
00:04:18,158 --> 00:04:20,693
Yes. And you are?

59
00:04:21,795 --> 00:04:24,298
I am William Herrera.

60
00:04:24,298 --> 00:04:29,469
I'll be supervising this project
on behalf of my brother, Vergil Herrera.

61
00:04:32,339 --> 00:04:35,175
So he's our boss.

62
00:04:35,175 --> 00:04:37,444
- I'm Megan Marcelo.
- Hi.

63
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:40,847
The executive producer of Idol.

64
00:04:40,847 --> 00:04:45,852
And this is our writer, Leroy del Mundo.

65
00:04:45,852 --> 00:04:49,623
And our creative assistant,
Ms. Deedee Fernandez.

66
00:04:49,623 --> 00:04:51,358
- Hello.
- Hello.

67
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:55,628
This is my executive assistant, Borj Rodrigo.

68
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,167
Sir, have some snacks.

69
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:05,405
- Have a seat, Sir.
- Thank you.

70
00:05:05,405 --> 00:05:07,241
- Thank you.
- Deedee.

71
00:05:07,241 --> 00:05:08,542
Yes.

72
00:05:08,542 --> 00:05:10,243
Here.

73
00:05:16,383 --> 00:05:17,517
Can I get some now?

74
00:05:17,517 --> 00:05:20,520
- I'll have some of this.
- Yes, go ahead, Sir.

75
00:05:21,774 --> 00:05:23,090
It's good, Sir.

76
00:05:23,090 --> 00:05:24,658
It's my son's favorite.

77
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,360
- Oh, really?
- Yes.

78
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:28,194
Do you have a spoon?

79
00:05:29,196 --> 00:05:30,297
Boss.

80
00:05:30,297 --> 00:05:31,695
Thank you.

81
00:05:33,055 --> 00:05:35,301
Can we start the meeting?

82
00:05:35,936 --> 00:05:39,005
Okay, any updates?

83
00:05:42,172 --> 00:05:46,179
Leroy is finalizing the script, Sir.

84
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:51,951
And this is the casting for VLH's approval.

85
00:06:19,071 --> 00:06:21,281
Boss Bro.

86
00:06:21,281 --> 00:06:23,583
You don't know anyone, right?

87
00:06:25,952 --> 00:06:28,789
Guys, let's take a picture for documentation.

88
00:06:28,789 --> 00:06:30,157
Okay?

89
00:06:30,157 --> 00:06:32,823
Hashtag, Tristan-Savana Project.

90
00:06:32,823 --> 00:06:34,761
Smile!

91
00:06:34,761 --> 00:06:36,630
There. One more. Candid.

92
00:06:36,630 --> 00:06:37,898
Candid.

93
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,299
Okay.

94
00:06:43,704 --> 00:06:45,438
There you go.

95
00:06:47,739 --> 00:06:50,208
Boss Bro, don't you really know anyone?

96
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:54,448
Me, too.

97
00:06:54,448 --> 00:06:56,787
But it's okay.

98
00:06:56,787 --> 00:06:59,590
Let's fake it till we make it.

99
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:05,258
Sir, they appear in drama series.

100
00:07:05,258 --> 00:07:06,293
- Is that so?
- Yes.

101
00:07:06,293 --> 00:07:08,828
And the others are theater actors.

102
00:07:09,896 --> 00:07:12,099
We'll just do our research.

103
00:07:12,099 --> 00:07:13,367
I'll take a look at it.

104
00:07:13,367 --> 00:07:15,302
Yeah.

105
00:07:15,302 --> 00:07:16,336
By the way, guys,

106
00:07:16,336 --> 00:07:20,807
Congressman Ramon asked
if we could tweak the script

107
00:07:20,807 --> 00:07:24,044
to make it different from his previous movie.

108
00:07:24,044 --> 00:07:26,747
He thinks the stories are too similar.

109
00:07:26,747 --> 00:07:29,594
Okay, I can do it on my own.

110
00:07:30,350 --> 00:07:33,854
Bro, you probably haven't heard,

111
00:07:33,854 --> 00:07:37,657
but Sir Liam has a degree
in Creative Writing.

112
00:07:37,657 --> 00:07:39,493
My name is Leroy.

113
00:07:39,493 --> 00:07:41,922
And no. I'm not asking.

114
00:07:41,922 --> 00:07:43,963
Hey. What are you doing?

115
00:07:47,667 --> 00:07:51,437
I will consult with you, Sir Liam,
if I need to.

116
00:07:52,221 --> 00:07:53,521
Okay.

117
00:08:01,943 --> 00:08:03,250
Sir, please eat.

118
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:04,484
Sure.

119
00:08:06,353 --> 00:08:08,822
Savana, let's have a picture together!

120
00:08:34,596 --> 00:08:35,949
Deedee, right?

121
00:08:35,949 --> 00:08:37,884
Yes, Sir?

122
00:08:37,884 --> 00:08:41,650
Deedee, I need you to do something.

123
00:08:51,798 --> 00:08:53,600
Smile!

124
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,569
There you go. Okay.

125
00:08:55,569 --> 00:08:56,703
Thank you!

126
00:08:56,703 --> 00:08:59,806
- Thank you!
- One more, here.

127
00:09:00,482 --> 00:09:02,083
Here, too.

128
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:05,312
- That's enough.
- That's okay.

129
00:09:05,312 --> 00:09:06,613
Oh, sorry, Sir.

130
00:09:06,613 --> 00:09:08,300
Thank you.

131
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:09,724
Odet, stay here for now.

132
00:09:09,724 --> 00:09:11,785
Okay, sure.

133
00:09:11,785 --> 00:09:13,324
Savana.

134
00:09:15,568 --> 00:09:16,987
Have a seat.

135
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:21,061
Water? Juice? Brandy?

136
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:22,796
Let's talk.

137
00:09:22,796 --> 00:09:24,931
Yes, Savana, we're talking.

138
00:09:25,899 --> 00:09:28,134
I'll be honest with you.

139
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:31,270
I don't want to work with your brother.

140
00:09:32,286 --> 00:09:34,131
Liam?

141
00:09:34,131 --> 00:09:35,632
Yes.

142
00:09:37,530 --> 00:09:40,947
Well, we have a common ground.

143
00:09:40,947 --> 00:09:43,950
You're not the only one who doesn't like him.

144
00:09:44,628 --> 00:09:45,852
Great.

145
00:09:45,852 --> 00:09:49,558
I want a new creative manager for my film.

146
00:09:51,225 --> 00:09:53,126
Savana, listen.

147
00:09:53,126 --> 00:09:55,278
I didn't hire him.

148
00:09:55,278 --> 00:09:58,011
It was the company president's decision.

149
00:10:00,133 --> 00:10:04,304
But you run Blacksmith, right?

150
00:10:04,304 --> 00:10:07,974
Liam is non-negotiable, unfortunately.

151
00:10:09,876 --> 00:10:12,178
Then find a new actress.

152
00:10:12,178 --> 00:10:14,180
Savana!

153
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,649
Wait.

154
00:10:15,649 --> 00:10:17,783
Calm down, okay?

155
00:10:19,953 --> 00:10:21,988
Why don't you like Liam?

156
00:10:40,681 --> 00:10:44,044
<i>Our grandfather is still in jail.
He didn't do anything wrong.</i>

157
00:10:44,044 --> 00:10:47,080
<i>He only wants Casa Fuerte
to take responsibility</i>

158
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:50,417
<i>for everything they did to Verde Village.</i>

159
00:10:50,417 --> 00:10:53,019
<i>A lot of us lost our jobs and houses.</i>

160
00:10:53,019 --> 00:10:54,688
<i>The Herreras took everything from us!</i>

161
00:10:54,688 --> 00:10:57,668
<i>They took everything from us!</i>

162
00:11:02,162 --> 00:11:08,101
When I started in show business,
I promised only one thing...

163
00:11:08,101 --> 00:11:12,505
And that is to help the oppressed.

164
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:17,376
I will use my position and influence
to become their voice.

165
00:11:18,736 --> 00:11:22,949
Blacksmith has nothing to do with
whatever Liam did in Casa Fuerte.

166
00:11:22,949 --> 00:11:25,038
No, Vergil.

167
00:11:25,038 --> 00:11:27,281
You're a family.

168
00:11:28,121 --> 00:11:34,060
All your companies benefit
from the profits of Casa Fuerte.

169
00:11:35,128 --> 00:11:38,366
So, then... what do you want?

170
00:11:38,366 --> 00:11:40,501
I don't want to work with Liam Herrera.

171
00:11:40,501 --> 00:11:42,636
That's what I want.

172
00:11:48,209 --> 00:11:52,513
Hey. Pretty girl, what are you doing there?

173
00:11:52,513 --> 00:11:55,550
I want a selfie with Ms. Savana.

174
00:11:55,550 --> 00:11:57,652
- You want a picture, too?
- Yes.

175
00:11:57,652 --> 00:11:59,100
Okay, I'll tell her later.

176
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:00,187
- Later.
- Okay.

177
00:12:00,187 --> 00:12:02,123
Leave for now.

178
00:12:02,123 --> 00:12:03,653
Okay.

179
00:12:10,631 --> 00:12:12,333
What are they talking about?

180
00:12:12,333 --> 00:12:15,669
Sir, Savana wants you out of the project.

181
00:12:22,577 --> 00:12:25,580
Savana, wait.

182
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,581
What do you need this time?

183
00:12:30,451 --> 00:12:34,154
I just want to know why you're furious at me.

184
00:12:36,123 --> 00:12:38,458
I thought I already made it clear.

185
00:12:40,194 --> 00:12:44,697
Do I have to remind you, Liam Herrera,

186
00:12:44,697 --> 00:12:52,063
how many lives got ruined
because of your project in Casa Fuerte?

187
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:54,541
Liam, they are humans.

188
00:12:56,043 --> 00:13:02,049
They are humans,
not insects you can expel out of their homes.

189
00:13:08,422 --> 00:13:10,157
Look...

190
00:13:11,058 --> 00:13:13,761
Whatever it is I have done...

191
00:13:13,761 --> 00:13:15,129
I'm owning up to my mistakes.

192
00:13:15,129 --> 00:13:17,064
No, Liam.

193
00:13:17,999 --> 00:13:21,568
What is an apology without accountability?

194
00:13:23,971 --> 00:13:26,474
How can you say you own up to your mistakes

195
00:13:26,474 --> 00:13:29,576
when someone else suffers because of you?

196
00:13:31,112 --> 00:13:33,414
You know what, Savana...

197
00:13:33,414 --> 00:13:35,483
Like I said,

198
00:13:35,483 --> 00:13:39,487
Liam is a non-negotiable
to my father and Congressman Ramon.

199
00:13:39,487 --> 00:13:42,056
But as the saying goes,

200
00:13:42,056 --> 00:13:46,059
keep your friends close
and your enemies closer.

201
00:13:50,693 --> 00:13:53,200
What do you mean?

202
00:13:53,200 --> 00:14:00,474
Well, I think it's better that Liam is here,

203
00:14:00,474 --> 00:14:03,177
and not in Casa Fuerte.

204
00:14:03,177 --> 00:14:07,781
He won't be able to work on his pet project
in Verde Village.

205
00:14:08,916 --> 00:14:11,252
And while he's here,

206
00:14:11,252 --> 00:14:17,057
we can make his life a living hell,
until he gives up.

207
00:14:34,767 --> 00:14:36,334
[National Police]
[Sto. Cristo Police District]

208
00:14:36,813 --> 00:14:39,046
- Nestor Bartolome.
- Sir.

209
00:14:39,046 --> 00:14:40,915
You're free to go.

210
00:14:40,915 --> 00:14:42,188
What?

211
00:14:44,751 --> 00:14:46,352
Sir...

212
00:14:47,687 --> 00:14:49,288
Who bailed me out?

213
00:14:49,289 --> 00:14:52,830
The case against you has been dropped.

214
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:04,938
Grandpa?

215
00:15:05,773 --> 00:15:07,374
Grandson!

216
00:15:41,542 --> 00:15:46,346
Thank you for dropping the case
against my grandfather.

217
00:15:47,515 --> 00:15:51,317
Son, why are you thanking them?

218
00:15:51,317 --> 00:15:58,259
They are the reason
why almost all of Verde Village was wiped out.

219
00:15:58,259 --> 00:15:59,260
That's enough, Grandpa.

220
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:01,896
What matters now is you're free.
I'm really sorry.

221
00:16:01,896 --> 00:16:03,898
What do you mean free?

222
00:16:03,898 --> 00:16:06,901
It's a good thing
that I attacked this scumbag.

223
00:16:06,901 --> 00:16:10,571
If not, our house would have been demolished.

224
00:16:10,571 --> 00:16:12,794
Grandpa, please calm down.

225
00:16:12,794 --> 00:16:16,877
Please, hear my son out.

226
00:16:21,248 --> 00:16:22,674
Mister...

227
00:16:24,285 --> 00:16:29,055
First of all, I apologize
for what I did to Verde Village.

228
00:16:31,336 --> 00:16:33,137
Yes.

229
00:16:34,461 --> 00:16:37,364
I desired a good life.

230
00:16:38,809 --> 00:16:40,100
But I didn't realize

231
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:42,281
that it was at your expense

232
00:16:42,283 --> 00:16:46,085
and the residents of Verde Village.

233
00:16:48,274 --> 00:16:55,934
I know that I can't bring back
the lives and crops that were lost,

234
00:16:55,935 --> 00:16:58,411
no matter what I do.

235
00:17:00,387 --> 00:17:04,458
But I promise you,

236
00:17:05,359 --> 00:17:12,499
I will do everything
to find you a new home and livelihood.

237
00:17:12,499 --> 00:17:17,637
For you and the rest of Verde Village.

238
00:17:23,143 --> 00:17:25,312
Thank you.

239
00:17:26,714 --> 00:17:31,115
A lot of politicians have promised us
the same thing.

240
00:17:32,286 --> 00:17:35,522
I don't expect that you can do that.

241
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:42,286
But I believe
that your intentions are pure, kid.

242
00:17:42,286 --> 00:17:46,132
So I forgive you.

243
00:17:46,934 --> 00:17:51,004
I hope you can also forgive me
for what I did to you.

244
00:17:54,174 --> 00:17:56,276
Thank you so much.

245
00:18:18,732 --> 00:18:21,602
I'm so proud of you, son.

246
00:18:21,602 --> 00:18:23,833
I never thought that you could do that

247
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:26,667
because of everything that happened.

248
00:18:27,741 --> 00:18:31,678
I'm glad someone knocked some sense into me.

249
00:18:32,479 --> 00:18:34,281
You know...

250
00:18:35,449 --> 00:18:39,353
Even if you take the wrong path,

251
00:18:39,353 --> 00:18:46,359
your heart will lead you to the right way.

252
00:18:48,762 --> 00:18:50,667
But Mom,

253
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:55,238
I'm worried that the livelihood project
I'm planning for Verde Village

254
00:18:55,238 --> 00:18:59,072
will deplete my life savings.

255
00:19:00,095 --> 00:19:03,210
You'll earn it again.

256
00:19:03,210 --> 00:19:05,145
You're good.

257
00:19:08,649 --> 00:19:11,352
But what if there's an emergency?

258
00:19:11,352 --> 00:19:14,788
What if you get sick again?

259
00:19:14,788 --> 00:19:17,557
Sir, Ma'am, good morning.

260
00:19:18,792 --> 00:19:20,260
Good morning.

261
00:19:21,662 --> 00:19:24,732
Son, there's always a way.

262
00:19:24,732 --> 00:19:30,236
And if it's already your time,
you can't do anything about it.

263
00:19:31,591 --> 00:19:33,540
And...

264
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:41,028
from what I saw,
I think my job as a mother is done.

265
00:19:42,049 --> 00:19:44,585
Mom, don't talk like that.

266
00:19:44,585 --> 00:19:46,353
I'm serious.

267
00:19:48,355 --> 00:19:50,524
Just pray, son.

268
00:19:50,524 --> 00:19:52,492
Keep on praying.

269
00:20:09,009 --> 00:20:12,666
Miss Savana, have some palabok.

270
00:20:14,681 --> 00:20:17,117
Okay, sequence 17.

271
00:20:17,117 --> 00:20:19,186
Exterior. Bar. Night.

272
00:20:19,186 --> 00:20:21,555
Cindy is being harassed by some men.

273
00:20:21,555 --> 00:20:24,858
Chito will arrive
like a knight in shining armor.

274
00:20:24,858 --> 00:20:26,427
How dare you!

275
00:20:26,427 --> 00:20:29,530
The woman is helpless,
yet you are harassing her?

276
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:31,532
The man harassing the woman will laugh.

277
00:20:31,532 --> 00:20:33,300
He will glare at Chito.

278
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:35,369
A fight ensues.

279
00:20:35,369 --> 00:20:36,737
This is good.

280
00:20:36,737 --> 00:20:38,739
I like how it was written.

281
00:20:38,739 --> 00:20:41,542
And the fight scenes are also good.

282
00:20:41,542 --> 00:20:43,216
Poor Cindy.

283
00:20:43,216 --> 00:20:45,138
Luckily, Chito's there.

284
00:20:45,138 --> 00:20:48,382
Helpless Cindy thanks her savior.

285
00:20:48,382 --> 00:20:50,191
- Luckily...
- Stop!

286
00:20:51,752 --> 00:20:53,853
This is not right.

287
00:20:53,853 --> 00:20:55,055
Huh?

288
00:20:55,055 --> 00:20:56,890
The scene is good.

289
00:20:56,890 --> 00:20:58,659
I'm going to save you, right?

290
00:20:58,659 --> 00:21:00,594
That's the point.

291
00:21:00,594 --> 00:21:02,362
That's the problem.

292
00:21:04,565 --> 00:21:06,667
That's what sells.

293
00:21:06,667 --> 00:21:09,169
This will be among your list of hit movies.

294
00:21:10,104 --> 00:21:15,175
Helpless woman saved by her leading man.
That's a formula.

295
00:21:17,311 --> 00:21:19,212
I need no saving.

296
00:21:20,347 --> 00:21:24,884
We, women, need no saving.

297
00:21:26,954 --> 00:21:30,290
How this movie is written...

298
00:21:30,290 --> 00:21:35,195
should also show women
who can defend themselves.

299
00:21:37,364 --> 00:21:38,631
Right!

300
00:21:39,299 --> 00:21:41,502
Women empowerment.

301
00:21:41,502 --> 00:21:43,137
I also agree.

302
00:21:43,137 --> 00:21:45,472
Usually, Gen Z, like me,

303
00:21:45,472 --> 00:21:50,643
can identify more with strong,
independent female characters.

304
00:21:52,146 --> 00:21:56,950
Then talk to VLH, if that's what you want.

305
00:21:58,152 --> 00:22:00,687
Actually, I already talked to him.

306
00:22:00,687 --> 00:22:03,123
He approved my request, too.

307
00:22:04,358 --> 00:22:06,026
Wait.

308
00:22:06,026 --> 00:22:08,228
So you want to discard the whole material

309
00:22:08,228 --> 00:22:11,464
to accommodate Miss Savana's request?

310
00:22:13,371 --> 00:22:15,506
You need to think about my welfare, too.

311
00:22:16,503 --> 00:22:18,938
So you want me to start from scratch again?

312
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:23,177
New story, new characterization,
new screenplay.

313
00:22:23,177 --> 00:22:25,746
You need to pay me again.

314
00:22:25,746 --> 00:22:28,982
But this is the same project, Leroy.

315
00:22:28,982 --> 00:22:30,884
You were already paid for it.

316
00:22:30,884 --> 00:22:33,186
This is not the same project, Megan.

317
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:36,089
In principle,
this is already a different film.

318
00:22:38,158 --> 00:22:40,260
I understand that, Leroy.

319
00:22:44,865 --> 00:22:47,200
I don't think they can do it.

320
00:22:49,336 --> 00:22:52,706
Maybe you should get a new team, Liam.

321
00:22:52,706 --> 00:22:55,209
What I mean is...

322
00:22:55,209 --> 00:22:58,778
creative work should not be charity work.

323
00:23:00,247 --> 00:23:04,184
So Megan,
please prepare the budget for Leroy.

324
00:23:04,184 --> 00:23:06,587
And you have a strong point, too, Savana.

325
00:23:06,587 --> 00:23:08,855
Women empowerment...

326
00:23:08,855 --> 00:23:10,257
gender equality.

327
00:23:10,257 --> 00:23:11,658
You're right.

328
00:23:13,360 --> 00:23:15,272
So, Leroy,

329
00:23:15,272 --> 00:23:16,835
are you still willing to write

330
00:23:16,835 --> 00:23:20,367
for an additional half
of your professional fee?

331
00:23:20,367 --> 00:23:23,070
I'll take care of the other half.

332
00:23:23,070 --> 00:23:25,004
I will co-write with you.

333
00:23:31,545 --> 00:23:33,146
<i>It's true.</i>

334
00:23:33,146 --> 00:23:34,881
<i>It seems that in this story,</i>

335
00:23:34,881 --> 00:23:38,318
<i>you're not the princess
who always needs saving.</i>

336
00:23:38,318 --> 00:23:41,921
<i>You're a queen, and you needed no saving.</i>

337
00:23:42,801 --> 00:23:44,991
[Care in Paradise Orphanage]

338
00:23:44,992 --> 00:23:48,028
- Good evening.
- Good evening, everyone.

339
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:52,599
Good evening, Mother.
I'm sorry for coming late.

340
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:57,904
This is my fifth ribbon-cutting ceremony
for the day.

341
00:23:57,904 --> 00:24:01,366
It's okay, Congressman. No problem.

342
00:24:01,367 --> 00:24:02,608
Thank you so much.

343
00:24:02,608 --> 00:24:11,184
It's an honor to give public service
to those who need it.

344
00:24:11,184 --> 00:24:16,789
Especially to children
who are close to my heart.

345
00:24:18,158 --> 00:24:19,559
You know...

346
00:24:20,661 --> 00:24:26,033
I grew up on the streets, too.

347
00:24:26,033 --> 00:24:28,067
I lost my parents at an early age.

348
00:24:28,969 --> 00:24:33,607
I worked hard until I reached this position

349
00:24:33,607 --> 00:24:41,782
where I can finally give back
and share my luck with others.

350
00:24:41,782 --> 00:24:48,421
Thank you so much for inviting me here.

351
00:24:49,156 --> 00:24:54,961
We should thank you
for the building you put up for the kids.

352
00:24:54,961 --> 00:24:56,663
Thank you so much.

353
00:24:56,663 --> 00:25:00,467
You're welcome. You're welcome, Mother.

354
00:25:00,467 --> 00:25:02,235
Thank you so much again.

355
00:25:02,235 --> 00:25:04,137
Thank you.

356
00:25:04,137 --> 00:25:06,673
Here it is, Congressman.

357
00:25:17,718 --> 00:25:19,686
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

358
00:25:19,686 --> 00:25:22,422
Congressman, for you.

359
00:25:23,183 --> 00:25:25,652
Thank you so much.

360
00:25:39,339 --> 00:25:41,007
Thank you.

361
00:25:41,007 --> 00:25:42,976
Thank you all.

362
00:25:46,380 --> 00:25:47,841
Congressman?

363
00:25:49,282 --> 00:25:51,451
Congressman, we need to go.

364
00:26:21,047 --> 00:26:25,652
<i>People ask, who do I wake up for?</i>

365
00:26:25,652 --> 00:26:28,388
<i>But here I am, asking...</i>

366
00:26:28,388 --> 00:26:31,190
<i>Who do I stay up late for?</i>

367
00:26:33,827 --> 00:26:38,165
<i>I never imagined
I would be a passionate writer again.</i>

368
00:26:38,165 --> 00:26:40,100
<i>All I remember is the time</i>

369
00:26:40,100 --> 00:26:45,172
<i>when I was
with my wife, Joyce, and my son, Dex.</i>

370
00:26:45,172 --> 00:26:47,440
<i>It seems so long ago.</i>

371
00:27:06,860 --> 00:27:09,229
<i>I always bear this in mind.</i>

372
00:27:09,229 --> 00:27:11,390
<i>That I need to be strong.</i>

373
00:27:11,390 --> 00:27:14,968
<i>Because when you love and like what you do,</i>

374
00:27:14,968 --> 00:27:17,927
<i>you have a clear reason to fight.</i>

375
00:27:31,718 --> 00:27:33,186
Where am I?

376
00:27:34,087 --> 00:27:36,097
Let me go.

377
00:27:37,330 --> 00:27:39,398
Why am I tied up?

378
00:27:51,404 --> 00:27:52,841
Who are you?

379
00:27:54,107 --> 00:27:55,741
Who are you?

380
00:28:03,283 --> 00:28:04,584
Congressman?

381
00:28:05,852 --> 00:28:09,356
Congressman. Congressman, I'm glad you came.

382
00:28:09,356 --> 00:28:10,456
Hey!

383
00:28:11,091 --> 00:28:12,292
Untie me.

384
00:28:12,292 --> 00:28:13,827
The congressman is here now.

385
00:28:13,827 --> 00:28:16,129
Keep quiet.

386
00:28:16,129 --> 00:28:17,964
Congressman, are they your men?

387
00:28:17,964 --> 00:28:20,700
I think they took the wrong guy.

388
00:28:22,435 --> 00:28:25,839
I said, keep quiet!

389
00:28:39,119 --> 00:28:40,553
Congressman...

390
00:28:43,123 --> 00:28:45,558
They didn't make a mistake.

391
00:28:50,235 --> 00:28:55,467
I ordered them to bring you here.

392
00:28:55,467 --> 00:28:57,237
Why?

393
00:28:58,177 --> 00:29:00,840
Congressman, I'm loyal to you.

394
00:29:00,841 --> 00:29:03,977
That's why you trust me, right?

395
00:29:07,314 --> 00:29:10,583
That's my mistake.

396
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:16,055
I trusted you fully.

397
00:29:17,424 --> 00:29:20,393
I gave you complete trust!

398
00:29:23,797 --> 00:29:27,700
Where's the rest of the money
from the transaction in Magallanes?

399
00:29:28,354 --> 00:29:29,721
What?

400
00:29:31,230 --> 00:29:33,632
That's 20 million pesos.

401
00:29:34,458 --> 00:29:39,259
Do you think I forgot about it?

402
00:29:39,267 --> 00:29:41,032
- Huh?
- Congressman...

403
00:29:41,033 --> 00:29:43,749
Congressman, I don't know
what you're talking about.

404
00:29:43,750 --> 00:29:45,618
I don't know anything about that...

405
00:29:46,854 --> 00:29:48,988
I don't know anything.

406
00:29:57,570 --> 00:29:58,737
Congressman?

407
00:29:59,264 --> 00:30:00,868
Congressman, what are you going to do?

408
00:30:00,868 --> 00:30:02,469
Congressman.

409
00:30:02,469 --> 00:30:03,637
Congressman, what's that?

410
00:30:03,637 --> 00:30:05,433
What are you going to do with me?

411
00:30:05,434 --> 00:30:06,782
Congressman!

412
00:30:06,782 --> 00:30:09,762
Congressman, I don't know
what you're talking about.

413
00:30:09,763 --> 00:30:12,414
Congressman, I'm begging you!

414
00:30:13,380 --> 00:30:15,548
Congressman, have mercy.

415
00:30:15,548 --> 00:30:17,220
Congressman.

416
00:30:17,220 --> 00:30:18,766
Congressman!

417
00:30:21,821 --> 00:30:23,438
Congressman.

418
00:30:26,802 --> 00:30:28,328
Hold on, Congressman!

419
00:30:28,328 --> 00:30:29,596
Wait!

420
00:30:29,596 --> 00:30:31,164
My mother got sick.

421
00:30:31,164 --> 00:30:33,967
No. No. It was my grandfather.

422
00:30:33,967 --> 00:30:37,037
Congressman, I will pay you back.

423
00:30:37,037 --> 00:30:38,672
There's still money left.

424
00:30:38,672 --> 00:30:41,341
I will have my wife get it.

425
00:30:41,341 --> 00:30:43,843
Congressman, please stop.

426
00:30:44,944 --> 00:30:46,546
Congressman.

427
00:30:46,546 --> 00:30:49,315
- Congressman.
- That's all I want to hear.

428
00:30:50,316 --> 00:30:53,119
For you to tell the truth.

429
00:30:57,123 --> 00:30:59,859
But I know where you live.

430
00:31:02,095 --> 00:31:06,532
I'll let my men get the money.

431
00:31:08,768 --> 00:31:11,203
I don't want to bother you.

432
00:31:12,639 --> 00:31:14,907
It would be too much.

433
00:31:17,610 --> 00:31:23,048
Congressman, leave my family alone.

434
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:25,517
Congressman, keep my family out of this!

435
00:31:25,517 --> 00:31:26,986
Congressman!

436
00:31:31,502 --> 00:31:33,960
Congressman, no!

437
00:31:33,960 --> 00:31:36,262
I'm begging you, Congressman! No!

438
00:31:52,912 --> 00:31:54,347
Congressman.

439
00:31:54,347 --> 00:31:55,782
Congressman.

440
00:31:55,782 --> 00:31:57,317
Congressman.

441
00:31:58,185 --> 00:31:59,541
Congressman.

442
00:32:42,128 --> 00:32:44,563
Now you know what will happen...

443
00:32:45,465 --> 00:32:48,234
if you do the same thing.

444
00:33:21,768 --> 00:33:22,968
Sir?

445
00:33:23,703 --> 00:33:25,771
Sorry, but...

446
00:33:31,322 --> 00:33:34,191
Unbelievable. She still doesn't like it?

447
00:33:36,650 --> 00:33:38,418
I'm sorry, Megan.

448
00:33:41,755 --> 00:33:43,523
It's okay, Sir.

449
00:33:44,124 --> 00:33:48,409
I saw the effort you made the whole night.

450
00:33:48,410 --> 00:33:52,076
It's not a common sight here in Blacksmith.

451
00:33:52,078 --> 00:33:56,282
We haven't seen someone work hard
as much as you do in a long while.

452
00:33:57,502 --> 00:33:58,770
Oh, boy.

453
00:33:59,459 --> 00:34:02,361
I should thank you instead.

454
00:34:02,362 --> 00:34:07,233
You stayed with me the whole night.

455
00:34:09,922 --> 00:34:11,856
We have to, Sir.

456
00:34:12,352 --> 00:34:14,826
Single mom representative.

457
00:34:17,724 --> 00:34:21,694
And, Leroy...

458
00:34:21,694 --> 00:34:23,897
he has so many debts to pay.

459
00:34:23,897 --> 00:34:26,899
He's the breadwinner of his family.

460
00:34:28,435 --> 00:34:32,831
Deedee, on the other hand,
is a working student.

461
00:34:32,832 --> 00:34:35,267
Career-oriented.

462
00:34:36,173 --> 00:34:41,345
It's nice because even if they're sleeping,

463
00:34:41,347 --> 00:34:44,295
their passion is very much awake.

464
00:34:44,297 --> 00:34:47,066
The passion of this creative team.

465
00:34:51,891 --> 00:34:53,192
Megan...

466
00:34:54,537 --> 00:34:56,038
Don't worry.

467
00:34:56,663 --> 00:34:58,932
I'll work on this.

468
00:34:58,932 --> 00:35:04,270
And let them sleep for now.

469
00:35:04,270 --> 00:35:09,174
And maybe you should go home.

470
00:35:09,174 --> 00:35:11,910
I'm sure your kid misses you already.

471
00:35:11,910 --> 00:35:13,745
Yes, Sir.

472
00:35:13,745 --> 00:35:17,982
By the way, where's Savana?

473
00:35:28,427 --> 00:35:31,763
You were so good earlier.
Your scene with Savana was so great.

474
00:35:31,763 --> 00:35:34,666
- You're very good in...
- Bye. Thank you so much.

475
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:36,322
I enjoyed the shoot today.

476
00:35:36,322 --> 00:35:38,003
Take care.

477
00:35:38,003 --> 00:35:39,082
- Bye.
- Bye!

478
00:35:39,082 --> 00:35:42,507
Very good. You're so great. We'll meet again.

479
00:35:42,507 --> 00:35:44,409
- Savana?
- When is your next filming schedule?

480
00:35:44,409 --> 00:35:45,744
- Saturday.
- Saturday?

481
00:35:45,744 --> 00:35:47,812
Can we set things straight?

482
00:35:50,382 --> 00:35:52,884
What do you need this time, Liam?

483
00:35:58,290 --> 00:36:00,658
What do you really want, Savana?

484
00:36:02,727 --> 00:36:04,562
I already said it.

485
00:36:05,564 --> 00:36:09,701
I want an empowered character.

486
00:36:09,701 --> 00:36:12,771
Is what we wrote
not empowering enough for you?

487
00:36:12,771 --> 00:36:18,576
We've addressed all your comments,
and all your requests already.

488
00:36:20,879 --> 00:36:23,381
Something still seems wrong.

489
00:36:29,287 --> 00:36:30,588
Wrong?

490
00:36:32,491 --> 00:36:35,494
Savana, what don't you like about it?

491
00:36:35,494 --> 00:36:37,596
Tell me what you don't like.

492
00:36:37,596 --> 00:36:40,298
Or is it because you want your role
to become more relevant than Tristan's?

493
00:36:40,298 --> 00:36:42,334
You.

494
00:36:42,334 --> 00:36:45,135
You are what's wrong, Liam.
Isn't that clear to you?

495
00:36:45,135 --> 00:36:46,905
I don't want to work with you.

496
00:36:46,905 --> 00:36:48,306
See?

497
00:36:48,306 --> 00:36:51,610
My team is having a hard time
because of your personal hatred.

498
00:36:51,610 --> 00:36:53,778
You keep the project hanging.

499
00:36:54,513 --> 00:36:56,848
Savana, don't you realize?

500
00:36:56,848 --> 00:37:00,685
Everyone's job is affected because of you.

501
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:05,122
Megan...

502
00:37:05,123 --> 00:37:08,793
Megan is supporting her kid's schooling.

503
00:37:08,793 --> 00:37:11,029
Leroy is a breadwinner.

504
00:37:11,029 --> 00:37:14,699
Deedee is saving up money for her tuition.

505
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:17,201
And you, you're toying with us.

506
00:37:18,170 --> 00:37:21,606
Savana, you're so unprofessional.

507
00:37:21,606 --> 00:37:23,608
I hope you feel guilty.

508
00:37:25,443 --> 00:37:26,878
I'm sorry.

509
00:37:29,381 --> 00:37:31,683
If you really hate me that much,

510
00:37:31,683 --> 00:37:34,385
why did you accept this project?

511
00:37:35,320 --> 00:37:37,889
Because I am bound by the contract.

512
00:37:39,224 --> 00:37:40,758
How about you?

513
00:37:41,626 --> 00:37:44,495
Why do you insist on writing a movie?

514
00:37:46,231 --> 00:37:49,333
Because I wanted to be
given a second chance...

515
00:37:52,237 --> 00:37:57,842
To prove that I could still do
what I really want.

516
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:02,414
To correct the mistakes I made.

517
00:38:02,414 --> 00:38:05,250
Are we still talking about the script?

518
00:38:05,250 --> 00:38:07,318
I've paid for it already.

519
00:38:08,820 --> 00:38:11,089
And I know I will continue to pay for it

520
00:38:11,089 --> 00:38:13,691
as long as I am trapped in this situation.

521
00:38:14,759 --> 00:38:18,830
So if you're telling me
that you're trapped, Joyce...

522
00:38:22,767 --> 00:38:24,635
I mean, Savana.

523
00:38:26,404 --> 00:38:30,842
Let's work together to break free
and to create a decent output.

524
00:38:40,785 --> 00:38:42,087
Okay, bye. Bye.

525
00:38:42,087 --> 00:38:43,955
Bye, Auntie.

526
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:48,481
Okay, Savana, let's go home.

527
00:38:49,394 --> 00:38:51,429
Savana?

528
00:38:51,429 --> 00:38:52,865
Where is she going?

529
00:38:52,865 --> 00:38:54,533
Savana!

530
00:38:54,533 --> 00:38:56,702
Come back here.

531
00:38:56,702 --> 00:38:58,336
Savana!

532
00:39:08,814 --> 00:39:10,849
- Savana.
- Hi, Savana!

533
00:39:10,849 --> 00:39:12,384
- Hi, Savana!
- Hi, Chuchi.

534
00:39:12,384 --> 00:39:14,887
Hey, there's Savana!

535
00:39:14,887 --> 00:39:16,488
- So pretty.
- Hi, Savana!

536
00:39:16,488 --> 00:39:17,823
How are you, MJ?

537
00:39:17,823 --> 00:39:19,691
I'm okay.

538
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:27,066
- Hi, Savana.
- Hello.

539
00:39:27,066 --> 00:39:28,666
Savana, please buy some of this.

540
00:39:28,666 --> 00:39:30,635
Savana, buy from me, please.

541
00:39:30,635 --> 00:39:33,738
I'll come back later. Make it good.

542
00:39:33,738 --> 00:39:35,706
Yes, Ma'am.

543
00:39:41,579 --> 00:39:43,481
Grandpa Nestor?

544
00:39:43,481 --> 00:39:45,249
Savana!

545
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:49,087
I'm glad you came to visit.

546
00:39:49,087 --> 00:39:50,555
How are you, Grandpa?

547
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:52,224
When did they let you out of jail?

548
00:39:52,224 --> 00:39:54,059
Just the other day.

549
00:39:54,059 --> 00:39:56,428
Liam dropped the case against me.

550
00:39:56,428 --> 00:39:58,096
And not just that.

551
00:39:58,096 --> 00:40:01,867
He gave the residents of Verde Village
a livelihood,

552
00:40:01,867 --> 00:40:04,168
so we could start again.

553
00:40:05,804 --> 00:40:08,073
- Hey, eat first.
- Yes, Ma'am.

554
00:40:08,073 --> 00:40:10,776
- Dear, give her some.
- Here you go.

555
00:40:10,776 --> 00:40:12,446
Okay, cook more of it.

556
00:40:12,446 --> 00:40:13,658
Okay.

557
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:19,584
<i>He really paid for it.</i>

558
00:40:19,584 --> 00:40:22,154
<i>That scumbag did pay for it.</i>

559
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:40,105
<i>If you really are the reason
why I am here in this strange world,</i>

560
00:40:40,105 --> 00:40:43,274
<i>I won't be tired of looking for you.</i>

561
00:40:44,309 --> 00:40:47,078
<i>What magic did you bring into my life?</i>

562
00:40:49,081 --> 00:40:51,052
<i>Is it really magic?</i>

563
00:40:51,052 --> 00:40:53,084
<i>Why does it seem like a curse?</i>

564
00:41:28,153 --> 00:41:29,854
Mister?

565
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:34,679
Do you sell other antique typewriters
aside from the one on display?

566
00:41:34,679 --> 00:41:37,073
What kind of typewriter are you looking for?

567
00:41:37,073 --> 00:41:44,603
Something more rusty with a fading keyboard.

568
00:41:44,603 --> 00:41:50,328
The one I have has rust and fading keyboard.

569
00:41:51,102 --> 00:41:55,969
Maybe a little bigger than that.

570
00:41:56,782 --> 00:41:59,918
Why don't you buy the one on display?

571
00:41:59,918 --> 00:42:01,386
It's just the same.

572
00:42:01,386 --> 00:42:03,588
I can't do that, Mister.

573
00:42:03,588 --> 00:42:07,526
My life depends on
the typewriter I'm looking for.

574
00:42:07,526 --> 00:42:08,960
Is that so?

575
00:42:10,529 --> 00:42:12,030
You said life?

576
00:42:12,030 --> 00:42:14,379
How much is it? A million?

577
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:17,001
More than that.

578
00:42:18,036 --> 00:42:21,072
It has sentimental value.

579
00:42:21,072 --> 00:42:23,475
Let me get your number,

580
00:42:23,475 --> 00:42:28,546
so I can text you
if an old typewriter arrives.

581
00:42:29,614 --> 00:42:32,513
Okay. Thank you so much.

582
00:42:37,689 --> 00:42:39,091
Here you go.

583
00:42:40,292 --> 00:42:41,960
Okay. I'll text you.

584
00:42:41,960 --> 00:42:43,594
Thank you so much.

585
00:43:01,313 --> 00:43:04,315
What brings you here?
Make it quick. I'm busy.

586
00:43:06,184 --> 00:43:08,119
I know you don't want me here.

587
00:43:08,119 --> 00:43:09,420
You're right.

588
00:43:11,890 --> 00:43:14,725
- Brother...
- VLH.

589
00:43:17,229 --> 00:43:19,497
I came here as your brother.

590
00:43:21,333 --> 00:43:23,368
I brought this.

591
00:43:23,368 --> 00:43:25,136
Resignation letter.

592
00:43:30,275 --> 00:43:31,709
Irrevocable?

593
00:43:33,378 --> 00:43:34,879
Yes.

594
00:43:39,684 --> 00:43:41,786
Sir, I told her you're busy,

595
00:43:41,786 --> 00:43:44,122
but Miss Savana wants to talk to you.

596
00:43:44,122 --> 00:43:45,557
Of course, anytime.

597
00:43:45,557 --> 00:43:47,592
Savana, what can I do for you?

598
00:43:47,592 --> 00:43:50,128
Script, please.

599
00:43:50,128 --> 00:43:52,930
- What's this?
- I'm going to be part of this film.

600
00:44:01,006 --> 00:44:04,042
Well, if this is already okay with you,
I will now review it.

601
00:44:04,042 --> 00:44:06,138
In the meantime, give me and Liam a minute

602
00:44:06,138 --> 00:44:08,149
so we can talk about his resignation.

603
00:44:12,817 --> 00:44:15,220
Bro, it's a prank!

604
00:44:15,220 --> 00:44:17,088
Thank you so much for your time, Bro.

605
00:44:17,088 --> 00:44:20,423
Thank you so much.
I think we should go, Miss Savana.

606
00:44:20,423 --> 00:44:22,761
I'm excited about our look test.

607
00:44:22,761 --> 00:44:25,063
Sure.

608
00:44:25,063 --> 00:44:26,764
Bro!

609
00:44:37,742 --> 00:44:39,645
Pest!

610
00:44:53,291 --> 00:44:55,794
Thank you so much, Savana.

611
00:44:55,794 --> 00:44:58,729
But what made you change your mind?

612
00:45:01,766 --> 00:45:03,458
You, Liam.

613
00:45:04,269 --> 00:45:06,137
Me?

614
00:45:06,137 --> 00:45:08,041
Why me?

615
00:45:08,773 --> 00:45:11,443
Because you're right.

616
00:45:11,443 --> 00:45:15,775
Everyone deserves a second chance.

617
00:45:17,349 --> 00:45:21,319
I know that you helped the residents
of Verde Village.

618
00:45:23,021 --> 00:45:24,488
It's nothing.

619
00:45:24,488 --> 00:45:27,961
What is an apology
without accountability, right?

620
00:45:29,894 --> 00:45:32,430
I also want to apologize to you.

621
00:45:35,500 --> 00:45:37,501
For what?

622
00:45:39,163 --> 00:45:43,500
I just can't bear to see
people being oppressed.

623
00:45:47,012 --> 00:45:50,181
Thank you so much, too, Savana.

624
00:45:50,181 --> 00:45:52,547
Thank you for enlightening me.

625
00:46:02,694 --> 00:46:04,695
Am I interrupting something?

626
00:46:06,131 --> 00:46:07,331
Via.

627
00:46:08,266 --> 00:46:11,703
Another day is not the same as the other day.

628
00:46:11,703 --> 00:46:14,673
True queens fix each other's crowns.

629
00:46:14,673 --> 00:46:17,108
I'm not sure about others, though.

630
00:46:17,108 --> 00:46:19,064
Beware.

631
00:46:26,851 --> 00:46:28,719
Miss Savana?

632
00:46:29,652 --> 00:46:31,327
Let's go.

633
00:46:34,693 --> 00:46:37,561
Okay. Please fix that.

634
00:47:53,805 --> 00:47:55,162
Help!

635
00:47:56,565 --> 00:47:57,982
Savana!

636
00:48:05,802 --> 00:48:07,616
Sorry, why are you here?

637
00:48:07,618 --> 00:48:09,533
This is my condo.

638
00:48:09,534 --> 00:48:11,488
You almost got harmed, Savana.

639
00:48:11,489 --> 00:48:13,566
Luckily, Liam and I passed by.

640
00:48:13,567 --> 00:48:14,793
I'm sorry.

641
00:48:14,793 --> 00:48:17,395
- What do you think, Boss Bro?
- I think they should end up together.

642
00:48:17,395 --> 00:48:18,530
How, Liam?

643
00:48:18,530 --> 00:48:20,867
Tell her everything he did wrong.

644
00:48:20,868 --> 00:48:22,132
He'll suffer for it.

645
00:48:22,133 --> 00:48:24,136
He'll take all the woman's anger.

646
00:48:24,137 --> 00:48:25,334
The girl will see

647
00:48:25,334 --> 00:48:30,209
how much effort the man puts
into changing his ways.

648
00:48:33,631 --> 00:48:34,647
Oh my, crocodile!

649
00:48:34,648 --> 00:48:37,990
Have you been here long?

650
00:48:39,108 --> 00:48:40,694
Via...
